## JavaScript Architecture

### Module Structure

```
js/
├── main.js             → Entry point: form handlers and runComparison(), the one path every flow ends in
├── calculator.js       → Pure business logic: costs, ranking, and compare() (best offer, saving, market median)
├── config.js          → Configuration constants (VAT rates, fees, default power, providers)
├── data-date.js       → Footer: date of the prices and the stale notice (every page; imports nothing)
├── page-actions.js    → Copy button and its menu (every page; imports nothing)
├── sobre.js           → sobre.html's entry point (the copy menu); a file because the CSP runs no inline script
├── pdf-service.js     → Loads PDF.js (self-hosted in vendor/pdfjs/) and reads the invoice; computes nothing
├── ui-components.js    → UI component initialization (tabs, tooltips, dropdowns)
├── ui-handlers.js     → Logo, delete, About, show/hide results, the input pill
├── ui-renderer.js     → Result rendering and DOM manipulation
├── url-state.js       → The result's inputs in the URL (ADR-018): read, coerced, written
└── utils.js           → Data loading (offers.json, tar.json, meta.json date) and formatting helpers

vendor/
├── pdfjs/              → PDF.js 3.11.174 and its worker (npm pdfjs-dist, Apache-2.0), loaded only for a PDF
├── fonts/              → Inter woff2, latin and latin-ext subsets (SIL OFL 1.1), declared in css/tokens.css
└── phosphor/LICENSE    → MIT notice for the Phosphor icons inlined in each page's sprite (see Icons)
```

Third-party code is copied in, never loaded from a CDN, so nothing outside the site sees the page or
the invoice. A new vendored file names its version and licence here.

### Content Security Policy

Both pages carry a meta CSP that allows only `'self'` (ADR-024). No inline `<script>` or `<style>`,
no `style="…"` in the markup (setting `element.style` from a module is fine), and nothing from
another origin. A new script, stylesheet, font or image is a file in the repo, linked like the rest.

### Icons

Icons are an inline SVG sprite at the top of each page's `<body>`, so they paint with the HTML and
need no request (audit PERF-1: the old Phosphor web font painted icons about 3.5 s after the text on
Slow 4G). A page uses one as `<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#ph-NAME-duotone"/></svg>`;
`js/ui-renderer.js` builds the same with `createIcon()`. Each page's sprite holds only the symbols that
page uses.

- Phosphor icons: `@phosphor-icons/core` 2.1.1 (MIT, notice in `vendor/phosphor/LICENSE`), from
  `assets/duotone/NAME-duotone.svg` or `assets/regular/NAME.svg`. Symbol ids are `ph-NAME-duotone` and
  `ph-NAME`. To add one: copy the file's `<path>`s into a `<symbol id="…" viewBox="0 0 256 256">` in the
  sprite of each page that uses it, without `fill` attributes (the duotone back path keeps its
  `opacity="0.2"`).
- The header's Ω (`gw-omega`, both pages) is the app icon's glyph, Inter v20 greek at wght 500, as a
  path: the Inter subsets the pages serve have no Ω. `.logo-mark` sizes it to Inter's cap height.
- `.icon` (css/base.css) sets the 14 px size and `fill: currentColor`; a component rule only adds what
  differs (colour, opacity).
- ChatGPT and Claude marks (`brand-chatgpt`, `brand-claude`, copy menu), in black, the same pair as
  the delonghi-ds page actions: Phosphor's `open-ai-logo` (regular, same package and licence) and the
  Claude Spark from Anthropic's press kit (https://www.anthropic.com/press-kit). The Spark's viewBox
  is padded so it draws at 87.5 % of the slot, matching Phosphor's inset. Both are trademarks, used
  only to label the links to those services. Phosphor's mark is its own redrawing, not the file
  OpenAI supplies at https://openai.com/brand/ (which needs its usage terms accepted).

**Note**: The current implementation consolidates some functionality. Components like modals and toasts are implemented inline where needed, following the principle of simplicity over abstraction.

### Module Pattern

Each module exports clean public API with JSDoc comments:

```javascript
// calculator.js

/**
 * Calculate monthly cost for an offer
 * Implements full calculation with IEC, proper tariff splitting, and VAT
 * 
 * @param {Object} offer - Offer object from offers.json
 * @param {number} consumption - Consumption in kWh
 * @param {number} power - Power in kVA
 * @param {Object} distribution - Optional: actual consumption distribution for bi/tri tariffs
 * @returns {number} Monthly cost in euros (with VAT)
 * 
 * @example
 * const cost = calculateMonthlyCost(offer, 250, 4.6);
 * // Returns: 71.23 (€/month)
 */
export function calculateMonthlyCost(offer, consumption, power, distribution = null) {
  // Implementation...
}
```

**Key principles**:
- **Pure functions**: No side effects, same input = same output
- **Single responsibility**: Each function does one thing well
- **Composability**: Functions can be combined to build complex behavior
- **Documentation**: JSDoc comments explain purpose, parameters, return values

### Accessibility Utilities

```javascript
// a11y.js

/**
 * Traps focus within an element (for modals).
 * Returns cleanup function.
 */
export function trapFocus(element) {
  const focusable = element.querySelectorAll(
    'button, [href], input, select, textarea, [tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])'
  );
  const first = focusable[0];
  const last = focusable[focusable.length - 1];
  
  function handleKeydown(e) {
    if (e.key !== 'Tab') return;
    
    if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) {
      e.preventDefault();
      last.focus();
    } else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) {
      e.preventDefault();
      first.focus();
    }
  }
  
  element.addEventListener('keydown', handleKeydown);
  first?.focus();
  
  return () => element.removeEventListener('keydown', handleKeydown);
}

/**
 * Announces message to screen readers.
 */
export function announce(message, priority = 'polite') {
  const el = document.createElement('div');
  el.setAttribute('role', 'status');
  el.setAttribute('aria-live', priority);
  el.setAttribute('aria-atomic', 'true');
  el.className = 'sr-only';
  el.textContent = message;
  
  document.body.appendChild(el);
  setTimeout(() => el.remove(), 1000);
}

/**
 * Handles Escape key to close overlays.
 */
export function onEscape(callback) {
  function handler(e) {
    if (e.key === 'Escape') callback();
  }
  document.addEventListener('keydown', handler);
  return () => document.removeEventListener('keydown', handler);
}
```

### State Management

**Current implementation**: Tab-based state management with result caching

```javascript
// main.js

const state = {
  // Tab results cache
  tabResults: {
    estimate: null,
    precise: null
  },
  
  // Current active mode
  currentMode: 'estimate',
  
  // Manual form visibility
  manualFormVisible: false
};
```

**State flow**:
1. User submits form (estimate or precise)
2. Result is calculated and rendered
3. Result HTML is cached in `state.tabResults[mode]`
4. When switching tabs, cached result is reused (no recalculation)
5. When form is cleared, cache is cleared

**Future enhancement**: URL-based state encoding for bookmarkable/shareable results (see ADR-018 in DECISIONS.mdc)

**Benefits**:
- No localStorage dependency (works in private browsing)
- Stateless by default (can be enhanced with URL state)
- Fast tab switching (cached results)
- Simple implementation (no complex state library)

