## Installable App (PWA)

The site installs to the home screen and opens standalone (audit decision: full PWA; the offline
part is the service worker, ADR-023).

- `sw.js` (registered from `js/main.js` after `load`): pages and `data/*` network first, with the
  saved copy offline and a marked response that makes `js/data-date.js` show the offline notice;
  `vendor/*` cache first; other own files served from the cache and refreshed in the background.
  Its PRECACHE list must name every file in css/ and js/ (selftest checks), and `VERSION` is the
  price date, rewritten by the weekly refresh. Off on localhost unless the URL has `?sw`.

- `manifest.webmanifest`: name, `start_url` and `scope` `/`, `display: standalone`, background and
  theme `#E8E8E8` (the rendered page background), and the icons below. A manifest takes one theme
  colour only, so the per-theme colours live in the pages' `theme-color` metas: light `#E8E8E8`,
  dark `#1C241C`. Until dark mode exists (audit 4.16a) a dark phone shows a dark bar above the light page.
  Colours here are hex, not OKLCH: the manifest and the meta are read outside CSS.
- `icons/`: `favicon.svg`, `apple-touch-icon.png` (180, full bleed), `icon-192.png` and
  `icon-512.png` (rounded tile), `icon-maskable-512.png` (glyph inside the 80 % safe zone). The mark is
  the header's Ω drawn from Inter (v20 greek subset, weight 500, SIL OFL 1.1) in `#3E4D37` on
  `#E8E8E8`, as an outline, so it never depends on a font. The PNGs are renders of the same SVG.
- Both pages link the manifest, the icons and the theme colours, and set `viewport-fit=cover`. With
  it, an installed page reaches the screen edges, so `body` pads by
  `env(safe-area-inset-*)` (0 on screens without a notch or home indicator).

