## Performance Budget

The only copy of the budget. Sizes are gzip, as the server sends them (1 KB = 1,000 bytes), and
`scripts/size-check.js` checks this table in the gate. It reads the limits from here and owns which
files each row counts. To raise a limit, change it here and give the reason in the commit.

<!-- size-check -->
| Row | What it counts | Limit |
|-----|----------------|-------|
| `index.html` | the page, with its icon sprite | 16 KB |
| `sobre.html` | the page, with its icon sprite | 16 KB |
| `CSS` | every file in css/, summed | 32 KB |
| `JavaScript` | every file in js/, summed | 40 KB |
| `Landing page` | index.html, all CSS and JS, and Inter latin | 150 KB |
<!-- /size-check -->

Not counted: PDF.js (`vendor/pdfjs/`, about 378 KB gzip) loads only when someone picks a PDF;
`data/offers.json` loads on submit and its bounds live in `scripts/validate-data.js`; Inter latin-ext
loads only for characters outside Portuguese.

Time targets, measured with the audit's lab method (Slow 4G, 4x CPU, HTTP/2): first contentful paint
about 1.8 s or less, with every icon on that first frame.

